  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="PT">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="PT">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="PT">N&#xfa;mero de setores produtivos chave com regulamenta&#xe7;&#xe3;o e procedimentos padronizados e harmonizados com a lei de ABS e o Protocolo de Nag&#xf3;ia;
N&#xfa;mero de cadastros e notifica&#xe7;&#xf5;es/ano no SisGen;
N&#xfa;mero de  homens e mulheres representantes de povos ind&#xed;genas, povos e comunidades tradicionais e agricultores familiares, da academia, empresas e do governo, capacitados.
Percentual de cumprimento do Plano de Trabalho Anual (PTA) estabelecido para o Projeto.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2018">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="PT">Embora o Brasil tenha uma nova legisla&#xe7;&#xe3;o nacional sobre ABS desde 2015, faz se necess&#xe1;ria a readequa&#xe7;&#xe3;o de institui&#xe7;&#xf5;es e de infraestrutura organizacional, e de tecnologia para superar algumas barreiras que impedem a aplica&#xe7;&#xe3;o efetiva da nova legisla&#xe7;&#xe3;o e dos seus regulamentos, bem como o aperfei&#xe7;oamento do conhecimento dos agentes p&#xfa;blicos, provedores e usu&#xe1;rios desses recursos, permitindo que o pa&#xed;s cumpra os termos do Protocolo de Nag&#xf3;ia e da Conven&#xe7;&#xe3;o sobre Diversidade Biol&#xf3;gica.</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="PT">Targets to be reached by the end of the project:
1.	Nagoya Protocol (NP) ratified by the legislative authority
2.	3 approved regulations
3.	5 sectors harmonized with the Nagoya Protocol
4.	410 visits to the ABS portal
5.	9,119 cumulative registrations and notifications on SisGen
6.	232 male and female representatives from academia, companies and the government trained per year.
7.	300 male and female representatives of indigenous peoples, traditional peoples and communities and family farmers trained per year.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="PT">1.	International seminar on best practices postponed to 2021 due to COVID19 restrictions.
2.	3 newly approved regulations (1 resolution, 1 technical orientations and 1 deliberation);
3.	5 sectors harmonized with the Nagoya Protocol;
4.	Following national partner instructions, data and information related to the ABS system will be available under the Ministry of Environment website (no longer its website). The page was under restructure in 2020.
